//? Title: Gated PixelCNN: Two Causal Streams
//? Subtitle: Explicit gates, class-table offsets and controlled raster sampling
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A vertical stream can carry information that a plain masked convolutional stack
cannot reach. A horizontal stream combines that information with earlier pixels
on the current row. This compact native Gated PixelCNN uses three width-four
blocks with paired tanh/sigmoid gates, then a Bernoulli head. Both an image-only
model and a class-conditioned model are fitted on the same binary8x8 MNIST
protocol. Worked masks and gates precede the real data. The complete program
shows all192 Adam writes and every raster-sampling step. Fixed-final test losses
are.58265 and.57816 bits per binary pixel, both worse than the fit-only
Bernoulli baseline's.38445. Full causal Jacobians, an opened blind spot and
shared-noise class controls establish the model's dependency protocol, not
realistic generation or superior likelihood.
)
\toc

> Keep vertical and horizontal information separate

[van den Oord et al., Conditional Image Generation with PixelCNN Decoders
(2016)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.05328) combines gated convolutional layers
with conditioning information. This teaching variant uses three small dual-stream
blocks, one gray binary channel and ten possible digit classes. It is trained
from scratch, without pretrained weights, normalization, dropout or pooling.

The vertical stream at row r sees only raw rows above r. Its first3x3 mask
allows the top kernel row; later vertical masks allow the top and current
feature rows. This is safe because the current vertical feature row already
excludes the current raw row. A1x3 horizontal stream sees earlier sites in
the current row, plus a1x1 projection from the gated vertical stream. The first
horizontal mask allows only the left kernel cell; later masks also allow the
center causal hidden feature. Thus every output remains independent of its
current and future raw pixels, while vertical links can fill the ordinary
masked-CNN blind spot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpc_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
