> Hand-check four structural masks

The top two panels below show vertical first/later masks; the bottom panels
show horizontal first/later masks. Gray cells outside the central horizontal
row are unused drawing space: the actual horizontal kernels have height1.
All mask channels repeat the same spatial structure. The first masks exclude
the whole current raw pixel, including all channels in a future RGB context.

For binary input, block0 has48 forbidden vertical weights and16 forbidden
horizontal weights. Each later width4 block has96 forbidden vertical and32
forbidden horizontal coordinates. The total is320. They remain stored but are
multiplied by stopped structural zeros inside the graph, so their partials are
exactly zero. The source's unconditional model has1073 values in23 leaves;
six learned10x8 class tables add480 values and6 leaves, giving1553/29.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpc_masks.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
 for(bool vertical:{true,false})for(bool first:{true,false}){
  auto mask=m::GatedPixelMask(1,vertical,first,1);
  if(!vertical)mask=n::concat({n::full({1,3,1,1},.5),mask,n::full({1,3,1,1},.5)},0);
  panels.push_back(n::image_grid(n::reshape(mask,{9,1,1,1}),3,3,.5,40));
 }
 n::save_image_grid(n::stack(panels),"build/gpc_masks.png",2,0,1,10,.5,1);
 std::print("Binary source: block0 masked48+16; later blocks2*(96+32); total320.\n");
}
