> Inspect binary inputs and preserve the baseline comparison

Both variants receive exactly the same prepared images and row ordering. The
first fit rows below show resized gray values above their exact binary thresholds.
The fit-only independent Bernoulli baseline uses q_j=(count_j+.5)/1001,
evaluating held-out NLL with the **unrounded Double posterior**. Its archived
probabilities are separately Float32; using those rounded values for the scalar
would alter the original protocol.

