> Verify strict causality and the opened blind spot separately

Each variant differentiates all64 logits with respect to all64 raw input sites.
Every current/future entry k>=j is exactly zero. Each site also flips all current
and future bits simultaneously and requires every conditional through j to
remain bit identical. These128 finite-change guards complement8192 Jacobian
entries; a zero local derivative alone could hide a ReLU or saturation issue.
Single-image predictions match the same image inside the full test batch.

The source blind-spot probe uses logit34(row4,col2) and input28(row3,col4).
A plain masked PixelCNN cannot connect these sites; the gated vertical stream
can. The source's plain comparison has its initial seed8401 weights, while the
two gated comparisons use their fitted final weights. It is a dependency
check, not a fitted-loss comparison or causal attribution to the digit label.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpc_blindspot.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 std::vector<n::Tensor> gradients;std::vector<std::string> names{"Plain initial","Gated image-only","Gated conditional"};
 for(const std::string variant:{"unconditional","conditional"}){
  std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> a;
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/gated_pixel_cnn/"+variant+"/blindspot.npz"))a.emplace(key,value);
  if(variant=="unconditional")gradients.push_back(n::reshape(a.at("plain_input_gradient"),{64}));
  gradients.push_back(n::reshape(a.at("gated_input_gradient"),{64}));
 }
 const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colours{{100,116,139},{37,99,235},{220,38,38}};
 auto all=n::stack(gradients);double lo=n::min(all).item(),hi=n::max(all).item(),range=hi-lo;
 for(int k=0;k<3;++k){
  auto values=gradients[k].to_vector<double>();
  plot.lines(n::arange(0,64).to_vector<double>(),values,names[k],colours[k]);
  plot.points({28},{values[28]},"",colours[k],6);
 }
 plot.y_limits(lo-.15*range,hi+.6*range).x_label("Raw input raster site; markers show site28")
 .y_label("Logit34 partial").title("The vertical link opens a previously unreachable past site")
 .save_svg("build/gpc_blindspot.svg");
 std::print("Input28 partial: plain={:.9f}, image-only={:.9f}, conditional={:.9f}.\n",gradients[0].to_vector<double>()[28],gradients[1].to_vector<double>()[28],gradients[2].to_vector<double>()[28]);
}
