> Hold the random streams fixed while changing the class

The class grid has ten rows, classes0..9, with four shared uniform streams per
row. An unconditional model must repeat the same four images on every row:
valid labels are ignored exactly. The conditional model may change its output
when the class changes, but a visible difference alone does not establish that
the generated image represents that class. The source includes every sample;
there is no selection of readable digits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpc_class_grid.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::vector<n::Tensor> groups;
 for(const std::string variant:{"unconditional","conditional"})
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/gated_pixel_cnn/"+variant+"/class_grid.npz"))if(key=="images")groups.push_back(n::reshape(value,{10,4,8,8,1}));
 auto image=n::reshape(n::concat(groups,1),{80,8,8,1});
 n::save_image_grid(n::tile(image,{1,1,1,3}),"build/gpc_class_grid.png",8,0,1,0,0,8);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/gpc_class_grid.png)
// result_end

\caption(Rows are classes0 through9. Left four columns: unconditional, repeating exactly under the four common streams. Right four: conditional, using the same streams and its learned class tables. Class effects are present, while image quality remains weak.)
\alttext(Ten rows show four repeated unconditional samples on the left and four class-conditioned samples on the right, under identical random streams.)

A second control keeps every test image fixed and shifts its supplied class
from c to(c+1)mod10. Unconditional probabilities remain bit identical. The
conditional model's maximum probability change over12800 sites is.0292038.
The class-wise means below average absolute changes within each true-class
pool; they measure sensitivity to this supplied label shift, not accuracy.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpc_class_effect.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int variant_index=0;
 const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colours{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}};
 for(const std::string variant:{"unconditional","conditional"}){
  std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> data,out,control;
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/gated_pixel_cnn/"+variant+"/data.npz"))data.emplace(key,value);
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/gated_pixel_cnn/"+variant+"/outputs.npz"))out.emplace(key,value);
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/gated_pixel_cnn/"+variant+"/class_controls.npz"))control.emplace(key,value);
  auto delta=n::mean(n::abs(n::cast(control.at("probability"),n::DType::Float64)-n::cast(out.at("probability"),n::DType::Float64)),{1,2,3});
  auto labels=data.at("test_labels").to_vector<std::int32_t>();std::vector<double> means;
  for(int c=0;c<10;++c){std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;for(int i=0;i<200;++i)if(labels[i]==c)rows.push_back(i);means.push_back(n::mean(n::take_rows(delta,rows)).item());}
  plot.lines(n::arange(0,10).to_vector<double>(),means,variant_index?"Conditional":"Image-only",colours[variant_index]);++variant_index;
 }
 plot.y_limits(-.0005,.026).x_label("Original test digit class").y_label("Mean absolute probability change")
 .title("Changing the supplied class affects only the conditional model").save_svg("build/gpc_class_effect.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/gpc_class_effect.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The image-only curve is exactly zero. The conditional curve averages per-pixel probability changes after shifting the supplied class, grouped by original test class. It is a controlled input-sensitivity measurement, with the image held fixed.)
\alttext(A blue image-only line stays at zero across classes0..9; a red conditional line is positive, showing a response to the changed supplied class.)

> Keep numerical fidelity separate from generative quality

Both final checkpoints restore every named leaf exactly. A separate development
NumPy oracle checks553830 forward values,257348 analytic partials,152 scalar
finite differences, all192 Adam writes, all6000 fitting-row visits,8192 input
Jacobian entries,128 future-flip guards and15872 sampled pixels. It verifies
complete uniform-bank layout, prefix preservation, shared four-stream class
controls, unconditional label invariance and both blind-spot probes. The report
must reproduce all50 original archives/3231050 values and576 phase captures
before the old executable is retired. Source checks do not require TensorFlow
or a different checkout at runtime.

The result is a faithful, small experiment in gated causal image densities.
Both gated models retain a worse fixed-final likelihood than the fit-only
baseline. Their slight difference in held-out loss does not isolate class
conditioning from parameter count or initialization. The class controls verify
that a supplied label has an effect only when enabled; neither that effect nor
the samples establish classification accuracy, perceptual realism or full-paper
PixelCNN performance.

